 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Things already done",
     "texto": [
      "Past passive participles are usually formed from perfective transitive verbs and describe the result: **прочитанная книга**, **написанное письмо**. The full forms agree in gender, number and case with the Russian noun: **книга** is feminine.",
      "Common endings are **-нн-** and **-т-**: **прочитать → прочитанный**, **написать → написанный**, **открыть → открытый**. Not all verbs form the participle regularly; learn the common forms in context."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The short form",
     "texto": [
      "As a predicate, the passive participle usually takes the short form: **дверь закрыта**, **письмо написано**, **окно открыто**. It agrees in gender and number, but the short form does not decline for case.",
      "Imperfective verbs can also form present passive participles, such as **читаемый** (being read); they appear mainly in formal registers. At B1 it is useful to recognise them even though they are practised less."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
